cachy-asahi-release-tools 0.4.0-1

Project launcher, packaging and tests: cachy-asahi contributors, MIT.
The portable endpoint transport and dependency manifest are retained byte-for-byte
from PR396 source head a6a9f947f889175925b86c4e8b337d116429bd28,
merged as cb90e05e1ffbf262353a874a5b598aa1939799b3. Its seven-file
endpoint-copy/verifier closure is unchanged. Each file's exact origin revision,
path, size, SHA-256 and installed location is in source-provenance.json.
The prior 0.2 launcher and seven private helper files are separately retained
byte-for-byte with their frozen source profiles and existing copyright notices.
Test-only archives preserve complete prior 0.2 and 0.3 recipes and local sources;
they are excluded from the installed payload. All retained project files are
under the included MIT LICENSE. No project-runtime license exception was found
in this finite set.

Python, zstd, GnuPG, libarchive and pacman are external package dependencies,
not vendored or relicensed here. Their licenses and notices remain their own.
TEST keys, generated fixture packages and modeled hardware observations confer
no production trust, native execution, installation or release acceptance.
